# Allowlist. `COPY . /src/` in the Dockerfile pulls the whole build context
# into the builder layer, so anything not needed to run `vite build` — local
# artefacts, credentials, editor state — must never enter it.
#
# Everything is excluded first; the `!` rules below re-add exactly the build
# inputs. Keep this in sync when a new top-level build input appears.
*
**/.*

# --- build inputs ---------------------------------------------------------
!package.json
!package-lock.json
!.npmrc
!index.html
!vite.config.js
!build.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!config.json
!docker-nginx.conf
!src
!public
# `npm run build` fetches the patched call widget for this queue first.
!element-call
!scripts

# --- belt and braces ------------------------------------------------------
# Re-excluded after the allowlist so a future `!` rule cannot leak them.
.git
.github
.secrets
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
element-call/dist
element-call/dist.partial
coverage
*.log
.env
.env.*
*.keystore
*.jks
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.asc
*.gpg
id_rsa*
.DS_Store
